    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d91">

                <pb facs="0236" n="140" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg140"/>

                <head>No. 78.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Borges.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-03-03"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 3,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your note of the 23d of
                    February, 1878, on the subject of making provision by law for the punishment of
                    counterfeiting paper money of foreign governments, and to your notes of June 25
                    and November 8 last, relating to the same subject, I have the honor to inclose
                    herewith a copy of a letter in regard to the matter from the chairman of the
                    Senate Committee on the Judiciary.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d91-a1.xml" xpointer="d91-a1"/>
            </div>
